<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Feature SiLA2Version="1.0" FeatureVersion="2.0" MaturityLevel="Draft" Originator="org.riken"
         Category="instruments"
         xmlns="http://www.sila-standard.org"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.sila-standard.org https://gitlab.com/SiLA2/sila_base/raw/master/schema/FeatureDefinition.xsd">

  <Identifier>PanTiltController</Identifier>
  <DisplayName>Pan Tilt Controller</DisplayName>
  <Description>
    Pan/tilt movement and position presets of the camera (via ONVIF PTZ).

    Coordinate system (angles in degrees):
      Origin (Pan 0, Tilt 0): the direction the camera faces after power-up, i.e. the side of the
        camera body with the logo. MoveHome returns to it.
      Pan : positive = turn to the LEFT as seen from behind the camera (counter-clockwise viewed from
            above, for a camera standing on a table). Negative = turn to the right.
            In the camera image, positive pan turns the view to the left: objects in the image move
            to the right. A person facing the camera sees it turn to their right.
            Example: to turn 90 degrees to the left, use MoveRelative with DeltaPan = +90.
      Tilt: positive = UP, negative = DOWN. In the image, positive tilt moves objects down.
      Movement range: see the MovementRange property. On a Tapo C232 it is Pan -170 to +170
        (340 degrees mechanical range) and Tilt -34.5 to +34.5 (69 degrees).
      A target outside the movement range is not an error: the camera stops at the limit.
      Check the returned position.

    Accuracy: the camera works in a unitless -1 to +1 space; this server converts linearly using the
    mechanical range of the model (server options --pan-range-deg / --tilt-range-deg, Tapo C232 values
    by default). On a Tapo C232 this was only roughly confirmed by eye (Pan -85 to +85 looked like about
    170 to 180 degrees). Treat angles as approximate, to within several degrees. Positions are reported
    rounded to 0.1 degree. The product page also states "360 degrees pan / 110 degrees tilt"; those are
    the visible coverage including the lens field of view, not the movement range. For a
    ceiling-mounted camera the directions may be inverted (not verified).

    Movement behavior (Tapo C232):
      The camera moves pan first, then tilt. Pan speed is about 32 degrees per second; a full pan sweep
      (340 degrees) takes about 11 seconds, plus up to about 5 seconds of tilt.
      Movement commands finish only when the camera has stopped, and return the final position
      (Position) and the position before the movement (StartPosition). To go back to where the camera
      was before a movement, use MoveAbsolute with that StartPosition; MoveHome instead goes to the
      power-up front (Pan 0, Tilt 0).
      Only one movement can run at a time; a movement command issued while another is running is
      rejected with MovementInProgress. Snapshots and recordings may run during movements.

    Presets: at most 8 presets can be stored in the camera (Tapo C232). Presets are identified by a
    token assigned by the camera and have a name chosen by the user. Preset names are unique on this
    server: saving with an existing name updates that preset.
  </Description>

  <Command>
    <Identifier>MoveAbsolute</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Move Absolute</DisplayName>
    <Description>
      Move to an absolute pan/tilt position in degrees from the power-up front (positive = left / up)
      and wait until the camera has stopped. A target outside MovementRange stops at the limit.
      To keep one axis where it is, pass its value from CurrentPosition.
    </Description>
    <Observable>Yes</Observable>
    <Parameter>
      <Identifier>Pan</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Pan</DisplayName>
      <Description>Target pan in degrees. Positive = left, negative = right; 0 = power-up front.</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanAngle</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Parameter>
    <Parameter>
      <Identifier>Tilt</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Tilt</DisplayName>
      <Description>Target tilt in degrees. Positive = up, negative = down; 0 = power-up tilt.</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>TiltAngle</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Parameter>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>Position</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Position</DisplayName>
      <Description>Position after the movement.</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltPosition</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Response>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>StartPosition</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Start Position</DisplayName>
      <Description>Position before the movement (pass it to MoveAbsolute to go back).</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltPosition</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Response>
    <DefinedExecutionErrors>
      <Identifier>CameraCommunicationError</Identifier>
      <Identifier>InvalidInstrumentStatus</Identifier>
      <Identifier>MovementInProgress</Identifier>
    </DefinedExecutionErrors>
  </Command>

  <Command>
    <Identifier>MoveRelative</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Move Relative</DisplayName>
    <Description>
      Turn by the given angles in degrees from the current position (positive = left / up) and wait
      until the camera has stopped. Pass 0 for an axis that should not move.
      A target outside MovementRange stops at the limit (no error); check the returned position.
    </Description>
    <Observable>Yes</Observable>
    <Parameter>
      <Identifier>DeltaPan</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Delta Pan</DisplayName>
      <Description>Pan change in degrees. Positive = left, negative = right; 0 = keep the pan.</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanOffset</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Parameter>
    <Parameter>
      <Identifier>DeltaTilt</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Delta Tilt</DisplayName>
      <Description>Tilt change in degrees. Positive = up, negative = down; 0 = keep the tilt.</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>TiltOffset</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Parameter>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>Position</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Position</DisplayName>
      <Description>Position after the movement.</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltPosition</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Response>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>StartPosition</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Start Position</DisplayName>
      <Description>Position before the movement (pass it to MoveAbsolute to go back).</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltPosition</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Response>
    <DefinedExecutionErrors>
      <Identifier>CameraCommunicationError</Identifier>
      <Identifier>InvalidInstrumentStatus</Identifier>
      <Identifier>MovementInProgress</Identifier>
    </DefinedExecutionErrors>
  </Command>

  <Command>
    <Identifier>MoveHome</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Move Home</DisplayName>
    <Description>Move to Pan 0, Tilt 0 (the power-up front direction) and wait until the camera has stopped.</Description>
    <Observable>Yes</Observable>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>Position</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Position</DisplayName>
      <Description>Position after the movement.</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltPosition</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Response>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>StartPosition</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Start Position</DisplayName>
      <Description>Position before the movement (pass it to MoveAbsolute to go back).</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltPosition</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Response>
    <DefinedExecutionErrors>
      <Identifier>CameraCommunicationError</Identifier>
      <Identifier>InvalidInstrumentStatus</Identifier>
      <Identifier>MovementInProgress</Identifier>
    </DefinedExecutionErrors>
  </Command>

  <Command>
    <Identifier>GetPresets</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Get Presets</DisplayName>
    <Description>List the presets stored in the camera.</Description>
    <Observable>No</Observable>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>Presets</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Presets</DisplayName>
      <Description>Stored presets.</Description>
      <DataType>
        <List>
          <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>Preset</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
        </List>
      </DataType>
    </Response>
    <DefinedExecutionErrors>
      <Identifier>CameraCommunicationError</Identifier>
      <Identifier>InvalidInstrumentStatus</Identifier>
    </DefinedExecutionErrors>
  </Command>

  <Command>
    <Identifier>GotoPreset</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Go To Preset</DisplayName>
    <Description>Move to a stored preset and wait until the camera has stopped.</Description>
    <Observable>Yes</Observable>
    <Parameter>
      <Identifier>PresetToken</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Preset Token</DisplayName>
      <Description>Token of the preset (see GetPresets).</Description>
      <DataType><Basic>String</Basic></DataType>
    </Parameter>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>Position</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Position</DisplayName>
      <Description>Position after the movement.</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltPosition</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Response>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>StartPosition</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Start Position</DisplayName>
      <Description>Position before the movement (pass it to MoveAbsolute to go back).</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltPosition</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Response>
    <DefinedExecutionErrors>
      <Identifier>CameraCommunicationError</Identifier>
      <Identifier>InvalidInstrumentStatus</Identifier>
      <Identifier>MovementInProgress</Identifier>
      <Identifier>PresetNotFound</Identifier>
    </DefinedExecutionErrors>
  </Command>

  <Command>
    <Identifier>SavePreset</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Save Preset</DisplayName>
    <Description>
      Store the current position as a preset with the given name. If a preset with the same name
      already exists, its position is updated and its token is kept.
    </Description>
    <Observable>No</Observable>
    <Parameter>
      <Identifier>Name</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Name</DisplayName>
      <Description>
        Preset name: 1 to 32 bytes in UTF-8 (e.g. up to 32 ASCII characters or about 10 Japanese
        characters). The characters &amp; &lt; &gt; " ' are not allowed (the camera cannot handle them).
      </Description>
      <DataType>
        <Constrained>
          <DataType><Basic>String</Basic></DataType>
          <Constraints>
            <MinimalLength>1</MinimalLength>
            <MaximalLength>32</MaximalLength>
            <Pattern>[^&amp;&lt;&gt;"']+</Pattern>
          </Constraints>
        </Constrained>
      </DataType>
    </Parameter>
    <Response>
      <Identifier>Preset</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Preset</DisplayName>
      <Description>The saved preset.</Description>
      <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>Preset</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    </Response>
    <DefinedExecutionErrors>
      <Identifier>CameraCommunicationError</Identifier>
      <Identifier>InvalidInstrumentStatus</Identifier>
      <Identifier>PresetLimitReached</Identifier>
      <Identifier>InvalidPresetName</Identifier>
    </DefinedExecutionErrors>
  </Command>

  <Command>
    <Identifier>RemovePreset</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Remove Preset</DisplayName>
    <Description>Delete a stored preset.</Description>
    <Observable>No</Observable>
    <Parameter>
      <Identifier>PresetToken</Identifier>
      <DisplayName>Preset Token</DisplayName>
      <Description>Token of the preset (see GetPresets).</Description>
      <DataType><Basic>String</Basic></DataType>
    </Parameter>
    <DefinedExecutionErrors>
      <Identifier>CameraCommunicationError</Identifier>
      <Identifier>InvalidInstrumentStatus</Identifier>
      <Identifier>PresetNotFound</Identifier>
    </DefinedExecutionErrors>
  </Command>

  <Property>
    <Identifier>CurrentPosition</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Current Position</DisplayName>
    <Description>Current pan/tilt position in degrees from the power-up front (positive = left / up), as reported by the camera; it changes while moving.</Description>
    <Observable>No</Observable>
    <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltPosition</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
    <DefinedExecutionErrors>
      <Identifier>CameraCommunicationError</Identifier>
    </DefinedExecutionErrors>
  </Property>

  <Property>
    <Identifier>MovementRange</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Movement Range</DisplayName>
    <Description>
      The pan and tilt limits in degrees (Tapo C232: pan -170 to +170, tilt -34.5 to +34.5).
      They come from the server configuration (--pan-range-deg / --tilt-range-deg; Tapo C232 values
      by default), not from the camera.
    </Description>
    <Observable>No</Observable>
    <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanTiltLimits</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
  </Property>

  <DefinedExecutionError>
    <Identifier>CameraCommunicationError</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Camera Communication Error</DisplayName>
    <Description>The camera could not be reached or returned an error. The message contains details.</Description>
  </DefinedExecutionError>
  <DefinedExecutionError>
    <Identifier>InvalidInstrumentStatus</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Invalid Instrument Status</DisplayName>
    <Description>The command cannot be executed because the status is Not Connected or Error. Use Reset first.</Description>
  </DefinedExecutionError>
  <DefinedExecutionError>
    <Identifier>MovementInProgress</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Movement In Progress</DisplayName>
    <Description>Another movement command is still running. Wait for it to finish and retry.</Description>
  </DefinedExecutionError>
  <DefinedExecutionError>
    <Identifier>PresetNotFound</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Preset Not Found</DisplayName>
    <Description>No preset with the given token exists. Use GetPresets to list valid tokens.</Description>
  </DefinedExecutionError>
  <DefinedExecutionError>
    <Identifier>PresetLimitReached</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Preset Limit Reached</DisplayName>
    <Description>The camera cannot store more presets (8 on Tapo C232). Remove a preset first.</Description>
  </DefinedExecutionError>
  <DefinedExecutionError>
    <Identifier>InvalidPresetName</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Invalid Preset Name</DisplayName>
    <Description>The preset name is longer than 32 bytes in UTF-8.</Description>
  </DefinedExecutionError>

  <DataTypeDefinition>
    <Identifier>PanAngle</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Pan Angle</DisplayName>
    <Description>Pan in degrees from the power-up front, positive = left. The usable range is MovementRange.</Description>
    <DataType>
      <Constrained>
        <DataType><Basic>Real</Basic></DataType>
        <Constraints>
          <MinimalInclusive>-180</MinimalInclusive>
          <MaximalInclusive>180</MaximalInclusive>
          <Unit>
            <Label>deg</Label>
            <Factor>0.017453292519943295</Factor>
            <Offset>0</Offset>
            <UnitComponent>
              <SIUnit>Dimensionless</SIUnit>
              <Exponent>1</Exponent>
            </UnitComponent>
          </Unit>
        </Constraints>
      </Constrained>
    </DataType>
  </DataTypeDefinition>

  <DataTypeDefinition>
    <Identifier>TiltAngle</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Tilt Angle</DisplayName>
    <Description>Tilt in degrees from the power-up tilt, positive = up. The usable range is MovementRange.</Description>
    <DataType>
      <Constrained>
        <DataType><Basic>Real</Basic></DataType>
        <Constraints>
          <MinimalInclusive>-90</MinimalInclusive>
          <MaximalInclusive>90</MaximalInclusive>
          <Unit>
            <Label>deg</Label>
            <Factor>0.017453292519943295</Factor>
            <Offset>0</Offset>
            <UnitComponent>
              <SIUnit>Dimensionless</SIUnit>
              <Exponent>1</Exponent>
            </UnitComponent>
          </Unit>
        </Constraints>
      </Constrained>
    </DataType>
  </DataTypeDefinition>

  <DataTypeDefinition>
    <Identifier>PanOffset</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Pan Offset</DisplayName>
    <Description>Pan change in degrees, positive = left.</Description>
    <DataType>
      <Constrained>
        <DataType><Basic>Real</Basic></DataType>
        <Constraints>
          <MinimalInclusive>-360</MinimalInclusive>
          <MaximalInclusive>360</MaximalInclusive>
          <Unit>
            <Label>deg</Label>
            <Factor>0.017453292519943295</Factor>
            <Offset>0</Offset>
            <UnitComponent>
              <SIUnit>Dimensionless</SIUnit>
              <Exponent>1</Exponent>
            </UnitComponent>
          </Unit>
        </Constraints>
      </Constrained>
    </DataType>
  </DataTypeDefinition>

  <DataTypeDefinition>
    <Identifier>TiltOffset</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Tilt Offset</DisplayName>
    <Description>Tilt change in degrees, positive = up.</Description>
    <DataType>
      <Constrained>
        <DataType><Basic>Real</Basic></DataType>
        <Constraints>
          <MinimalInclusive>-180</MinimalInclusive>
          <MaximalInclusive>180</MaximalInclusive>
          <Unit>
            <Label>deg</Label>
            <Factor>0.017453292519943295</Factor>
            <Offset>0</Offset>
            <UnitComponent>
              <SIUnit>Dimensionless</SIUnit>
              <Exponent>1</Exponent>
            </UnitComponent>
          </Unit>
        </Constraints>
      </Constrained>
    </DataType>
  </DataTypeDefinition>

  <DataTypeDefinition>
    <Identifier>PanTiltPosition</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Pan Tilt Position</DisplayName>
    <Description>A pan/tilt position in degrees from the power-up front (see the feature description).</Description>
    <DataType>
      <Structure>
        <Element>
          <Identifier>Pan</Identifier>
          <DisplayName>Pan</DisplayName>
          <Description>Pan in degrees. Positive = left of the power-up front.</Description>
          <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanAngle</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
        </Element>
        <Element>
          <Identifier>Tilt</Identifier>
          <DisplayName>Tilt</DisplayName>
          <Description>Tilt in degrees. Positive = up.</Description>
          <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>TiltAngle</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
        </Element>
      </Structure>
    </DataType>
  </DataTypeDefinition>

  <DataTypeDefinition>
    <Identifier>PanTiltLimits</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Pan Tilt Limits</DisplayName>
    <Description>Pan and tilt limits in degrees (the type of the MovementRange property).</Description>
    <DataType>
      <Structure>
        <Element>
          <Identifier>PanMin</Identifier>
          <DisplayName>Pan Min</DisplayName>
          <Description>Rightmost pan (negative).</Description>
          <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanAngle</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
        </Element>
        <Element>
          <Identifier>PanMax</Identifier>
          <DisplayName>Pan Max</DisplayName>
          <Description>Leftmost pan (positive).</Description>
          <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>PanAngle</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
        </Element>
        <Element>
          <Identifier>TiltMin</Identifier>
          <DisplayName>Tilt Min</DisplayName>
          <Description>Lowest tilt (negative).</Description>
          <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>TiltAngle</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
        </Element>
        <Element>
          <Identifier>TiltMax</Identifier>
          <DisplayName>Tilt Max</DisplayName>
          <Description>Highest tilt (positive).</Description>
          <DataType><DataTypeIdentifier>TiltAngle</DataTypeIdentifier></DataType>
        </Element>
      </Structure>
    </DataType>
  </DataTypeDefinition>

  <DataTypeDefinition>
    <Identifier>Preset</Identifier>
    <DisplayName>Preset</DisplayName>
    <Description>A stored pan/tilt preset.</Description>
    <DataType>
      <Structure>
        <Element>
          <Identifier>PresetToken</Identifier>
          <DisplayName>Preset Token</DisplayName>
          <Description>Identifier assigned by the camera; use it with GotoPreset and RemovePreset.</Description>
          <DataType><Basic>String</Basic></DataType>
        </Element>
        <Element>
          <Identifier>Name</Identifier>
          <DisplayName>Name</DisplayName>
          <Description>User-defined name.</Description>
          <DataType><Basic>String</Basic></DataType>
        </Element>
      </Structure>
    </DataType>
  </DataTypeDefinition>

</Feature>
